Think of a for loop like a conveyor belt 🏭
Each item on the belt gets processed one by one — until the belt is empty.

For Loop = Do same task for every item!
The most used concept in DevOps Python — every script loops through servers, containers, files or commands! 🚀
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Summary Table

Feature           Code
------------------------------------------------
Basic loop        for item in collection

With index        for i, item in enumerate(list)

Number range      for i in range(5)

Dictionary        for k, v in dict.items()

Stop loop         break

Skip item         continue

Nested loop       loop inside loop

One line          [x for x in list]

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
🤔 What is For Loop?

Think of For Loop as an Assembly Line 🏭

Assembly line does SAME task
for EVERY item one by one

For Loop does SAME task
for EVERY item in collection

# Without loop - repetitive!
print("Deploying to web1...")
print("Deploying to web2...")
print("Deploying to web3...")
print("Deploying to web4...")
print("Deploying to web5...")

# With loop - clean!
servers = ['web1','web2','web3','web4','web5']
for server in servers:
    print(f"Deploying to {server}...")
